(d) FAIL. Rule 3 (the dashboard must parse `.skip` files "the same way" as the gate's first-match rule) and rule 8 (gate check exits 0 <=> derived.state === 'accepted') are broken by new CD4 code: gate.sh `skip_field` runs `sed "s/^KEY:[[:space:]]*//"` in the CALLER'S locale; parse.mjs `skipField` strips only ASCII space `[ \t\n\v\f\r]`. Under a UTF-8 locale (the operator's own: LANG=en_US.UTF-8) glibc's [[:space:]] also strips U+1680, U+2000-2006, U+2008-200A, U+2028/9, U+205F, U+3000. The gate is therefore locale-dependent and disagrees with the dashboard.
    Repro (runs from any copy of the tree; script kept at scratchpad/cd4-second/repro.sh): ledger row `k 2 tests,second,codex accepted 1`, valid checker-tests and checker-second PASS (correct MANIFEST_SHA256), and k.1.checker-codex.skip = `REASON: quota\nDETAIL: <U+2003 EM SPACE>\nTASK: k\nATTEMPT: 1\n`.
      LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8: gate check -> "FAIL: k: missing checker-codex evidence (attempt 1)", rc 1; dashboard derived.state = accepted   (dashboard LIES)
      LC_ALL=C:           gate check -> "OK: k accepted at tier 2", rc 0;                          dashboard derived.state = accepted
    Same with U+3000. Reverse direction: `REASON:<U+2003>quota` -> gate ACCEPTS (sed strips it), dashboard blocks. Reproduced with C.UTF-8 as well; POSIX/C locale agrees. `done` = `check` in every case.
    Remedy verified (rule-6 premise check): in a copy, changing skip_field's sed to `LC_ALL=C sed ...` makes my 69 skip-shape scenarios (incl. the three above) agree under en_US.UTF-8: "probe: 69 run, 0 mismatches". The harness cannot write such a record (its `skip()` maps a blank DETAIL to the reason), so this is reachable only by a hand-written/tampered record, but that is exactly what the anti-lie mirror exists for, and README.md now states "It agrees with `gate.sh check` by construction". Fix is local (one sed in gate.sh, or an explicit class on both sides) plus one pinned test (neither shipped suite nor the oracle has a non-ASCII-space fixture).
