OBSERVATIONS (not grounds for FAIL; backlog)
1. PRE-EXISTING gate/dashboard split, also in base: a trailing comma in the checks column (`tests,`, `tests,second,`; with Codex `tests,codex,`, `tests,second,codex,`). Gate's `read -ra` drops the empty trailing field and ACCEPTS; parse.mjs `split(',')` keeps it and BLOCKS (the conservative direction). Reproduced on basetree (pre-CD4 gate + parse): `base tc: tier 2 "tests,"` gate=ACC dash=blocked.
2. PRE-EXISTING header-whitespace split (SPEC CD-h): `FAMILY: crossvendor ` (trailing space) on a checker-codex verdict is invalid in the gate and valid in the dashboard (parseHeaderAndEvidence trims); same for `FAMILY: anthropic ` on checker-tests in the base. The Codex verdict inherits it; CD4 did correctly avoid it for .skip (first match, no trim).
3. CLAUDE.md lines 120-123: "at Tiers 2/3 whether or not codex is named (at Tier 1 only when named), it opens the dispute path, counts toward two consecutive fails, and counts in stats" reads as if the Tier-1 restriction covered all three; in fact an unnamed Tier-1 Codex FAIL still counts toward two-consecutive-fails escalation (probe: tier 1 unnamed FAILs at attempts 1 and 2 -> gate rejects with escalation, dashboard 'flagged') and in stats first-attempt. It mirrors the brief's rule 5/6 wording; imprecise, not false for acceptance.
4. swarm/codex-check.sh header (CD1, foreign, accepted) still says the gate recognises crossvendor / .skip "only after task CD4; until then do not point this at a live run's .swarm" - stale once CD4 lands; out of CD4's territory.
5. Oracle F13 / doc_test `all (lanes|agents|roles)( run)? on Claude` would not catch the wording "With every lane on Claude since 2026-08-19" that CLAUDE.md retains (it is qualified by "the Codex trial, below, adds a cross-vendor one", so not false).
6. The two additions beyond the brief (NUL byte invalidates a skip record; tier 2/3 verdict walk before the Codex evidence test) are consistent between gate and parse.mjs in every probe I ran (NUL mid-line and trailing -> both reject; invalid codex file + valid skip at tiers 1/2 -> both reject). The NUL addition is under-tested in the dashboard suite (P4).
7. `gate.sh stats` walks attempts 0..ledger attempt per row (pure bash); a ledger attempt of ~10^9 would make stats spin. Attempts are lead-set and hard-stop-bounded; noted only.
